From 7be6518287d8bb20b08c3e59f58c8f3707e36ae2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:02:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: clear object-detection panel flags on a new level

The new-level block in borg_update() cleared the per-panel
borg_detect_wall, borg_detect_trap, borg_detect_door and
borg_detect_evil flags but not borg_detect_obj, so object detection
stamped on a previous level's panel still counted after taking stairs:
the panel indices are positions, so the same panel on the new level
looked already-detected and the Borg skipped casting detect objects
there. Clear it with the others.
---
 src/borg/borg-update.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-update.c b/src/borg/borg-update.c
index 9c415ef12..6cd7a85e6 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-update.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-update.c
@@ -2144,6 +2144,7 @@ void borg_update(void)
                 borg_detect_trap[y][x] = false;
                 borg_detect_door[y][x] = false;
                 borg_detect_evil[y][x] = false;
+                borg_detect_obj[y][x] = false;
             }
         }
 
-- 
